  * pauses at the start) and draws the video itself into a CALayer, which is this
  * engine's platform layer. Its callbacks come from libVLC's threads; a bridge
  * object takes them to the main thread and drops them once the player is gone.
+ *
+ * Media bytes come from WebCore's loader (cookies, credentials, CORS, blob: and
+ * data: URLs, the page's referrer and user agent) and are handed to libVLC as a
+ * stream; libVLC asks for byte offsets when it seeks and the loader fetches them
